# Amazon Delivery Performance & Agent Efficiency Dashboard

## Project Title
**Amazon Delivery Performance & Agent Efficiency Dashboard**

## Project Overview
This project focuses on analyzing Amazon delivery operations using **MySQL, Power Query, DAX, and Microsoft Power BI**.

The dashboard provides insights into delivery performance, agent efficiency, order patterns, vehicle usage, weather and traffic conditions, delivery time, and order locations.

## Project Objectives
- Analyze overall delivery performance.
- Monitor total orders and delivery activity.
- Identify delivery delay patterns.
- Analyze performance by vehicle type.
- Evaluate delivery agent efficiency.
- Analyze traffic and weather impact.
- Analyze orders by month and order hour.
- Analyze delivery time and operational efficiency.
- Analyze store and delivery locations.
- Create an interactive Power BI dashboard.

## Tools & Technologies
- **MySQL** – Database and SQL analysis
- **Microsoft Power BI** – Dashboard and visualization
- **Power Query** – Data cleaning and ETL
- **DAX** – KPI and calculated measures
- **CSV** – Dataset source
- **Data Modeling** – Analytical model

## Dataset Description
The project uses an Amazon delivery dataset containing order, delivery, agent, vehicle, weather, traffic, location, and timing information.

The dataset contains approximately **10,000 delivery records**.

### Important Fields
- Order ID
- Order Date
- Order Time
- Pickup Time
- Delivery Time
- Agent ID
- Store Latitude
- Store Longitude
- Drop Latitude
- Drop Longitude
- Vehicle
- Weather
- Traffic
- Area

## SQL Analysis
MySQL is used as the database layer. SQL queries are used for aggregation and business analysis.

### Analysis Areas
- Total orders
- Orders by vehicle type
- Orders by weather
- Orders by traffic
- Orders by order hour
- Delivery time analysis
- Agent performance
- Location-based analysis

### Example Queries

```sql
SELECT COUNT(*) AS Total_Orders
FROM orders;
```

```sql
SELECT Vehicle_Type, COUNT(*) AS Total_Orders
FROM orders
GROUP BY Vehicle_Type;
```

## Power BI Dashboard
The Power BI solution contains **4 dashboard pages**.

### 1. Summary
Overall delivery performance with KPI cards and order analysis.

### 2. Delivery Performance
Analysis of delivery time, traffic, weather, vehicles, and delays.

### 3. Agent Performance
Analysis of agent efficiency, orders handled, and delivery performance.

### 4. Orders & Location Analysis
Analysis of orders by vehicle type, month, order hour, and store location.

## Key KPIs

| KPI | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Total Orders | Total number of delivery orders |
| Total Agents | Number of delivery agents |
| Average Delivery Time | Average delivery duration |
| Delayed Orders | Orders with delivery delays |
| On-Time Delivery | Delivery performance |
| Orders by Vehicle | Vehicle usage comparison |
| Orders by Weather | Weather-wise order distribution |
| Orders by Traffic | Traffic-wise order distribution |
| Orders by Hour | Peak ordering hours |

## Key Insights
- Identify peak order hours.
- Compare monthly order volumes.
- Analyze vehicle-wise order distribution.
- Understand traffic and weather effects.
- Identify delivery time patterns.
- Compare agent performance.
- Identify high-order locations.
- Support better delivery planning and resource allocation.

## Project Workflow

```text
Dataset Collection
       ↓
CSV Dataset
       ↓
MySQL Database
       ↓
SQL Analysis
       ↓
Connect MySQL with Power BI
       ↓
